public class TransactionManager implements ITransactionLookup {

    private final List<Transaction> allTransactions = new ArrayList<>();

    public void save(Transaction transaction) {
        allTransactions.add(transaction);
    }

    @Override
    public List<Transaction> getTransactionHistory() {
        System.out.println("fetching transaction history (slow lookup)...");
        return allTransactions;
    }
}

getTransactionHistory() hands back the field itself, not a copy. What can any caller do as a result?,Nothing - the list is final so it cannot be modified,"Anything: clear() it, remove individual transactions, or add fabricated ones - the manager's own records would change with no way for it to know","Only read it, because the method return type is List","Only add, not remove",,2,"final on the field stops the reference being reassigned

