A 6.00 item is paid with 1.00 in cash followed by 5.00 by card. Measured on the real code: the change reserve reads 53.5 before and 53.5 after. Where did the customer's 1.00 coin go, as far as the software is concerned?,It was refunded automatically at the end of the purchase,"Nowhere - the machine physically holds it but never recorded it, because the reserve decision is taken once at the end using only the LAST payment method, and CARD reports that it does not affect the reserve",It was counted twice and then cancelled out,It was added to the reserve but immediately paid back out as change,,2,"One decision, taken once, from one strategy - applied to a total that may have arrived through several different methods. Correct handling would have to track the cash portion of each individual payment.",2

